192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (Most space agencies today operate satellites using a centralized ground-based control system. For example, the Indian Space Research Organisation \(ISRO\) uses facilities such as the Master Control Facility \(MCF\) and the ISRO Telemetry, Tracking and Command Network \(ISTRAC\) to monitor and control satellites after they are launched. These systems handle everything from orbit adjustments and health monitoring to payload commands and station-keeping maneuvers for individual satellites like those in the INSAT, GSAT and IRNSS series, which are manually controlled from Earth stations.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 507 0 R
/E (Recent research confirms that automation and onboard autonomy are needed to manage task scheduling, decision-making, and coordination in distributed satellite systems.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
